    "body":  "## Summary\n\nPropose a same-identifier refresh of CA-SL v1alpha5. This does not introduce v1alpha6. The 2026-11-17 published baseline remains authoritative until this PR is reviewed and merged; the candidate then supersedes it under `connectionagent.io/v1alpha5`.\n\n## Normative decisions\n\n- Every Skill package has `SKILL.md`; `assurance/` is optional.\n- When Assurance is present, the complete source trio is `contract.yaml`, `procedure.yaml`, and `predicates.yaml`.\n- No Assurance means LLM-guided only and no Compiler invocation.\n- Valid Assurance enables both Deterministic and LLM-guided modes.\n- Invalid present Assurance is a hard import failure; never silently downgrade.\n- Add optional top-level `assurance/contract.yaml.when`, a pure CEL selector over `event.type` and typed `input`.\n- Keep `when` distinct from execution-time `predicates.yaml`.\n- Define formal match, unguarded SKILL.md semantic selection, fail-closed evaluation, and no legacy `applicability.when`.\n- Define source import/automatic build, compiled Artifact Inspect/Verify without rebuild, LLM Action without Compiler, and LLM-created Assurance source through the normal import path.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Same language identifier: `connectionagent.io/v1alpha5`.\n- No Domain/Task Contract Package, `supportedModes`, second LLM Contract, legacy compatibility, package signatures or Trust Registry.\n- Appendix M adds SA-001–SA-011 normative expectations.\n- The existing IngressCatalog and its diagnostic registry are unchanged.\n\n## Validation boundary\n\nThis PR updates normative documentation and the documentation validator only. It does **not** implement Compiler, Host, Runtime or Skill Importer behavior. The refreshed `contract.when` and Assurance-free import path must be implemented/verified by the Compiler/Host owners before product conformance can be claimed. CI results are pending and documentation checks do not imply product qualification.",
